infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title ROWS vs RANGE — the difference is ties
  desc Default is RANGE; for any running total write ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
  compares
    - label ROWS
      children
        - label Counts physical rows
          desc 1 PRECEDING means literally the one row before this one
        - label Each row adds its own amount
          desc Running total accumulates one row at a time, in order
        - label Correct on ties
          desc Tied sale_date rows never overcount the early ones
        - label Generally faster
          desc No need to scan ahead to find all peers
        - label Works with any ORDER BY
          desc Counts positions, so multi-column ORDER BY is fine
    - label RANGE
      children
        - label Operates on ORDER BY values
          desc CURRENT ROW means all rows with this row's value
        - label Ties are peers
          desc Same sale_date rows enter and leave the frame together
        - label Overcounts running totals
          desc Every tied row shows the same peer-inclusive total
        - label The silent default
          desc Inner ORDER BY with no frame = RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
        - label Needed for value frames
          desc INTERVAL '7 days' PRECEDING — single numeric/date column only
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
